\viewkind4\uc1\pard\cf1\ul\b\f0\fs24\'b6 Verse 1\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 1. O Come and mourn with me awhile;
\par O come ye to the Saviour's side;
\par O come, together let us mourn:
\par Jesus, our Lord, is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 2\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 2. Have we tears to shed for Him,
\par While soldiers scoff and Jews deride?
\par Ah! look how patiently He hangs:
\par Jesus, our Lord, is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 3\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 3. How fast His hands and feet are nailed,
\par His throat with parching thirst is dried!
\par His failing eyes are dim with woe:
\par Jesus, our Lord, is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 4\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 4. Seven times He spoke, seven words of love;
\par And all three hours His silence cried
\par For mercy on the souls of men:
\par Jesus, our Lord, is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 5\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 5. Come, let us stand beneath the Cross;
\par The fountain opened in His side
\par Shall purge our deepest stains away:
\par Jesus, our Lord, is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 6\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 6. A broken heart, a fount of tears,
\par Ask, and they will not be denied;
\par A broken heart love's cradle is:
\par Jesus, our Lord, is crucified.
\par 
\par \cf1\ul\b\'b6 Verse 7\cf0\ulnone\b0 
\par 7. O love of God! O sin of man!
\par In this dread act your strength is tried;
\par And victory remains with love:
\par For He, our Lord, is crucified.\f1 
\par \cf1\ul\b 
\par }

